/T (In a typical academic setting, a result has to be prepared after marks for individual subjects have been recorded. The marks are added to obtain a total, and the total is compared with the maximum possible marks to find the percentage. A grading rule is then applied, while the minimum passing requirement determines whether the student has passed. These steps are repeated for every result that needs to be prepared.)
/E (In a typical academic setting, a result has to be prepared after marks for individual subjects have been recorded. The marks are added to obtain a total, and the total is compared with the maximum possible marks to find the percentage. A grading rule is then applied, while the minimum passing requirement determines whether the student has passed. These steps are repeated for every result that needs to be prepared.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
