<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 174 0 R
/T (When the number of students is small, manual calculation may seem convenient. However, the same steps must be repeated carefully each time. A subject can be missed while adding marks, a total may be copied incorrectly, or a grade boundary may be applied inconsistently. Even a small arithmetic mistake can make the displayed result incorrect. A computer program can perform the same operations in the same order whenever it is given valid input.)
/E (When the number of students is small, manual calculation may seem convenient. However, the same steps must be repeated carefully each time. A subject can be missed while adding marks, a total may be copied incorrectly, or a grade boundary may be applied inconsistently. Even a small arithmetic mistake can make the displayed result incorrect. A computer program can perform the same operations in the same order whenever it is given valid input.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
