<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 203 0 R
/T (Every subject mark in this example is at least 33, so the student passes. The percentage of 80 meets the threshold for grade A. The output should therefore show the five subject marks, total 400/500, percentage 80.00%, grade A and status PASS. This example can be used during a demonstration because the arithmetic is easy to verify manually.)
/E (Every subject mark in this example is at least 33, so the student passes. The percentage of 80 meets the threshold for grade A. The output should therefore show the five subject marks, total 400/500, percentage 80.00%, grade A and status PASS. This example can be used during a demonstration because the arithmetic is easy to verify manually.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 203 0 R
/T (A second example checks the fail condition. If the marks are 95, 92, 88, 30 and 90, one subject is below the minimum passing mark. The program must display FAIL and grade F even though the total and percentage are high. This confirms that the program checks the subject-wise condition before assigning a passing grade.)
/E (A second example checks the fail condition. If the marks are 95, 92, 88, 30 and 90, one subject is below the minimum passing mark. The program must display FAIL and grade F even though the total and percentage are high. This confirms that the program checks the subject-wise condition before assigning a passing grade.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 203 0 R
/T (Invalid entries should also be tested. If the user enters the word 'abc', the program should display a message requesting a numeric value. If the user enters 105, it should explain that the mark must be between 0 and 100 and ask again. These cases show that the program is designed to handle mistakes in data entry instead of crashing or producing a misleading result.)
/E (Invalid entries should also be tested. If the user enters the word 'abc', the program should display a message requesting a numeric value. If the user enters 105, it should explain that the mark must be between 0 and 100 and ask again. These cases show that the program is designed to handle mistakes in data entry instead of crashing or producing a misleading result.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
