1140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 204 0 R
/T (Testing is an important part of software development because a program that runs without an error is not necessarily a program that produces the correct answer. Testing compares the actual output with the expected output for carefully selected inputs. For the Student Result Calculator, the tests should cover ordinary marks, grade boundaries, pass/fail conditions and invalid entries.)
/E (Testing is an important part of software development because a program that runs without an error is not necessarily a program that produces the correct answer. Testing compares the actual output with the expected output for carefully selected inputs. For the Student Result Calculator, the tests should cover ordinary marks, grade boundaries, pass/fail conditions and invalid entries.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 204 0 R
/T (A normal test uses marks such as 80, 90, 85, 75 and 70. The expected total is 400, the percentage is 80, the grade is A and the status is PASS. A subject-failure test uses at least one mark below 33 and checks that the result is FAIL even when the overall percentage is high.)
/E (A normal test uses marks such as 80, 90, 85, 75 and 70. The expected total is 400, the percentage is 80, the grade is A and the status is PASS. A subject-failure test uses at least one mark below 33 and checks that the result is FAIL even when the overall percentage is high.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 204 0 R
/T (Boundary testing focuses on values near the limits. Marks of 32 and 33 are especially important because they fall on opposite sides of the subject passing threshold. Grade-boundary tests should check percentages at and around 45, 60, 70, 80 and 90 to confirm that the if/elif conditions assign the intended grade.)
/E (Boundary testing focuses on values near the limits. Marks of 32 and 33 are especially important because they fall on opposite sides of the subject passing threshold. Grade-boundary tests should check percentages at and around 45, 60, 70, 80 and 90 to confirm that the if/elif conditions assign the intended grade.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 204 0 R
/T (Invalid-input testing includes text instead of a number, a negative mark and a mark above 100. The expected behaviour is that the program displays a helpful message and asks for a corrected value. A simple test table can record the input, expected result, actual result and whether the test passed. Testing should be repeated after any change to the code.)
/E (Invalid-input testing includes text instead of a number, a negative mark and a mark above 100. The expected behaviour is that the program displays a helpful message and asks for a corrected value. A simple test table can record the input, expected result, actual result and whether the test passed. Testing should be repeated after any change to the code.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [6]
