1862 0 obj
<<
/Title (The result of an examination is more than a collection of marks. It gives a student an idea of how well the topics have been understood and helps teachers communicate academic progress. Once marks are awarded, they must be totalled, converted into a percentage and interpreted according to the grading rules followed by the institution. Although these calculations are straightforward, repeating them for several subjects and students can become time-consuming.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1694 0 R
/Next 2051 0 R
>>
endobj
1863 0 obj
<<
/Title (The program is intended as an educational demonstration. It shows the basic logic behind result calculation, but it is not an official college result-management system. A real system may need student records, user accounts, secure storage, approval procedures and rules verified by the institution. The current project focuses on the calculation itself so that its working can be understood and explained clearly.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1694 0 R
/Prev 2052 0 R
>>
endobj
