2052 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project has been selected because it connects programming concepts with a familiar academic task. A student learning Python can see how input statements collect information, variables hold values, arithmetic operators perform calculations and conditional statements make decisions. Instead of treating these concepts as separate examples, the project brings them together in one complete program.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1694 0 R
/Prev 2051 0 R
/Next 1863 0 R
>>
endobj
2053 0 obj
<<
/Title (In a typical academic setting, a result has to be prepared after marks for individual subjects have been recorded. The marks are added to obtain a total, and the total is compared with the maximum possible marks to find the percentage. A grading rule is then applied, while the minimum passing requirement determines whether the student has passed. These steps are repeated for every result that needs to be prepared.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1864 0 R
/Next 2244 0 R
>>
endobj
2054 0 obj
<<
/Title (For a beginner, the project provides practice in breaking a problem into smaller tasks. The developer must decide what information is required, how the marks will be stored, which formula will be used and how the final grade will be chosen. These planning decisions are just as important as writing the code. Once the basic version works, it can be expanded gradually without changing the purpose of the original program.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1864 0 R
/Prev 2245 0 R
>>
endobj
