2057 0 obj
<<
/Title (Marks are educational information, so they should be handled responsibly. In this demonstration, the program runs locally and does not send marks to an online service. This keeps the implementation simple, but it does not remove the need to think carefully about data accuracy and privacy when the project is expanded.)
/Dest [45 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1865 0 R
/Next 2252 0 R
>>
endobj
2058 0 obj
<<
/Title (These considerations illustrate a general principle of software development: correct calculations are only one part of a reliable information system. The system must also handle data responsibly and make its limitations clear to the people using it.)
/Dest [45 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1865 0 R
/Prev 2253 0 R
>>
endobj
2059 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Student Result Calculator successfully demonstrates the calculation of total marks, percentage, grade and pass/fail status using the specified rules. With marks of 80, 90, 85, 75 and 70, the program calculates 400 out of 500 and a percentage of 80.00. Since every subject mark is at least 33, it assigns grade A and displays PASS.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1866 0 R
>>
endobj
